        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3e846f42-ba8d-5178-ab90-6e33f63312c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alec Guinness, David Lean, Santha Rama Rau, E. M. Forster\n- Films: Great Expectations, Oliver Twist, The Bridge on the River Kwai, Lawrence of Arabia, Doctor Zhivago, A Passage to India\n- Roles: Herbert Pocket, Fagin, Col. Nicholson, Prince Faisal, General Yevgraf Zhivago, Professor Godbole\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Actor\n- Works: A Passage to India play, A Passage to India novel\n\nFacts:\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on Great Expectations (1946) and played Herbert Pocket.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on Oliver Twist (1948) and played Fagin.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on The Bridge on the River Kwai (1957) and played Col. Nicholson.\n- Alec Guinness won the Academy Award for Best Actor for The Bridge on the River Kwai (1957).\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on Lawrence of Arabia (1962) and played Prince Faisal.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on Doctor Zhivago (1965) and played General Yevgraf Zhivago.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on A Passage to India (1984) and played Professor Godbole.\n- The screenplay of A Passage to India was based on Santha Rama Rau's play A Passage to India.\n- Santha Rama Rau's play A Passage to India was based on E. M. Forster's novel A Passage to India.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3be0a9f4-e66b-594e-891e-214a1a22f1e3",
        "text": "Page: Alec Guinness. Sentence: He is also known for his six collaborations with David Lean: Herbert Pocket in \"Great Expectations\" (1946), Fagin in \"Oliver Twist\" (1948), Col. Nicholson in \"The Bridge on the River Kwai\" (1957, for which he won the Academy Award for Best Actor), Prince Faisal in \"Lawrence of Arabia\" (1962), General Yevgraf Zhivago in \"Doctor Zhivago\" (1965), and Professor Godbole in \"A Passage to India\" (1984).\nPage: A Passage to India (film). Sentence: The screenplay is based on the play of the same name by Santha Rama Rau, which was based on the novel of the same name by E.M. Forster.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
